{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/766734-secret-passing","id":766734,"title":"Secret passing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-15T18:35:20-08:00","id":766734,"title":"Secret passing","content":"Do you make use of coded messages in your Demon games? coded may not really be the term I'm looking for, but I'm also thinking about a couple of ways of doing it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe best way to securely send a message would be encrypted, and I'd imagine that Demon's might have encryption beyond human means. Of course when I talk about encryption I don't think you'd actually expect the players to decrypt something.<br /> <br /> However one of the ways most portrayed in the media is &quot;code phrases&quot;. &quot;The Eagle has left the nest&quot;, or &quot;How's the weather?&quot;, &quot;It's sunny, but supposed to rain later&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also some popular ways (that aren't really considered secure) of hiding secret messages like giving someone numbers that references letters of text in the newspaper, or just leaving a classified ad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you use any of this in your Demon games? How do your Demon's get in touch with one another?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 11-15-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T08:04:54-08:00","id":767073,"title":"","content":"One group of demons in a game I was once in passed important messages to each other by sending a string of numbers through one of their telepathic Stigmatic allies. The first part of the string referenced the ISBN of a book, with the rest giving coordinates to a certain passage within, corresponding to a list of memorized code-phrases (which list was occasionally updated and reconfigured). It was very convoluted, built on paranoia and past bad experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T11:03:27-08:00","id":767159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/766734-secret-passing#post766734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do your Demon's get in touch with one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Special Message Embed is a good go-to for all of your encryption and 'how do demons communicate?' needs.<br /> <br /> Generally, the mastery of all living languages is enough to spoof investigators who aren't angels, especially if you use a nice mix of words from very, very different tongues/scripts. Euphenism helps for an extra level of security against angels, which can include code phrases too. Since demons will probably make use of modern communications technology (too inconvenient not to use a phone/the internet), which is very easy for the Machine to tap, this can be even more important, Factor in perfect recall and demonic codes and ciphers can be <i>incredibly</i> complex. <br /> <br /> I'm also fond of gadgets being used for messages. You can make one-shots that dissolve after being read (remind you of anything?), gadgets encoded with a message that can only be read/heard by a certain person (that might set other people on fire), messages that change to suit their readers..,<br /> <br /> A demon in one of my games has an Interlock they use to turn people into unknowingly messenger (see my signature). Generally, I find demonic communication really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T16:44:48-08:00","id":767426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/766734-secret-passing?p=767073#post767073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One group of demons in a game I was once in passed important messages to each other by sending a string of numbers through one of their telepathic Stigmatic allies. The first part of the string referenced the ISBN of a book, with the rest giving coordinates to a certain passage within, corresponding to a list of memorized code-phrases (which list was occasionally updated and reconfigured). It was very convoluted, built on paranoia and past bad experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eremite</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Special Message Embed</div> </div> </div> </div> is that in core or the players handbook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:19:24-08:00","id":767456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/766734-secret-passing?p=767426#post767426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is that in core or the players handbook?</div> </div> </div> </div>Corebook. Vocal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T22:14:24-08:00","id":767580,"title":"","content":"We use Numbers Stations. I established several existing in <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i>, along with their interval signals and other stuff like usual broadcast times. While impossible to decode, they can indicate increases in activity or a sign something they did got attention. The PCs have established their own, &quot;Countdown Lion&quot;, which starts off &quot;The Final Countdown&quot; and ends with &quot;The Lion Sleeps Tonight&quot;, both played on a Theremin. This was the players idea, and they were quite pleased for others.<br /> <br /> Info on a handout the players got. Most of them are based on specific real stations.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Numbers stations are a thing that exist in the world, but given Seattle is not Cold War Eastern Europe, an awful lot of them can be heard there. Some are doubtlessly in use by the God-Machine. Some may be used by Demons, indeed rumor has it the Saboteur Scarecrow maintains one of them. Some are no doubt maintained by enthusiasts that find them amusing. Some may have an even darker purpose.<br /> <br /> The Hot Cross Buns Station plays Hot Cross Buns as a station identifier, followed by a series of numbers. It can be heard at 8:30 PM, 11:30 PM, 3:30 AM, and 5:59 AM local time, and that set of transmissions is usually the same. The voice is either synthesized or an angel or demon in their true form. Hot Cross Buns is not known for unusual transmissions; it is suspected of being God-Machine because of its rigid schedule.<br /> <br /> The Naming Station has a mature woman with a Canadian accent reading much of the time. It got its name because instead of using the usual NATO phonetic characters, it uses American names, like Franklin or Peter. The names are consistent. The station is fond of zeros, and they appear generously in any set of numbers and letters. The reader says \u201cZero\u201d with an unusual sound to it, not sounding local or Canadian. Sets tend to be introduced by three (or occasionally two) names together, and tend to be sets of names and letters. No set schedule.<br /> <br /> The Warner Brothers Station communications in cartoon clips from Bugs Bunny, Yosemite Sam, and Roadrunner cartoons. There will be a quote from a character, followed by a series of numbers in text-to-speech. This station is extremely erratic, going months with no broadcasts and constant (different) ones in a given day. No letters are used.<br /> <br /> The NATO Station is similar to the Naming Station, with a younger woman and uses the NATO phonetic alphabet. It is more regular, airing at 6 and 12 am and pm every day, though most messages end in \u201cZero\u201d and when they don\u2019t, there is usually a slight tone of urgency to the speaker\u2019s voice. Messages going out at unusual times never end in \u201czero\u201d, suggesting the \u201czero\u201d ones are test or filler messages.<br /> <br /> The Magnetic Fields Station is similar to Hot Cross Buns, using Magnetic Fields by Jean-Michael Jarre as a station identifier, then a series of numbers. Names are occasionally used assumedly as phonetic letters, but different ones than the Naming Station uses, and much more rarely; never as a prefix. It only airs at Midnight with any regularity, when it airs at all.<br /> <br /> The Music Box Station, also known as the Satan Station, uses a music box as an identifier, and the numbers are read by a distorted little girl\u2019s voice. The voice is said to be \u201ca little unnerving\u201d to those who have heard it. It reads clusters of numbers and uses NATO phonetic characters, but changes \u201cDelta\u201d to \u201cDavid\u201d much like airlines that use that Alphabet do. It usually airs on 3s, 9s, and 6s, on the clock when it airs, but has no regular schedule.<br /> <br /> The Frogs Station sounds like a very loud synthesized frog croaking, sometimes more than one. It has no regular schedule; it may be silent for weeks, or go for hours. Like the Satan Station, it sounds unnerving, and extended listening can cause people to roll for a breaking point.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Numbers Stations will be coming up in my Crossover game<i> The Golden Eagle</i> as well, but not just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:03:29-08:00","id":767954,"title":"","content":"Also I wrote an encryption program (partly for the game and partly to attempt to learn Python) which takes a typed message as input. It then generates a cipher key based on the available characters coded for the program to utilize. Due to time and tech constraints (Windows 7 apparently will not allow me to properly use UTF-8), I was only able to make it work with the standard Western English character and number set. Brute force would easily break that. If UTF-8 would have worked however, I had a program that generated a cipher utilizing over 500 character combinations that would be unique to each message encrypted. Stupid Windows.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I intended to have for use with our game but got disgusted by my failed attempt to make the \u00fcber tool. \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":2668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","user":"Asmenedas","date":".  Left out info. 11-17-2015, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}